            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41065 implements this for \"func\" and \"expr\" options. \n\n\"prg\" options are less obvious but worth doing. Unlike \"expr\" options (which often are evaluated on a hot path, e.g. `foldexpr`), we can be less performance-sensitive with the approach to \"prg\" options: the legacy string form can be implemented as a Lua closure. So we can just always store Lua closures for \"prg\", which is helpful because they have weird, bespoke semantics which is difficult to express at the codegen level.",
            "created_at": "2026-07-31T10:30:50Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/18997#issuecomment-5141919858",
